  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1041 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nUncertainty remains for the end time for Saturday's activity. \nSome CAMs are hinting at additional activity later into the \nevening where others have things winding down around 7pm.\nMaintained low PoP during the 6PM-12AM timeframe to account for \nthis uncertainty. On Sunday, though still hot, the cold front will\nallow for drier air to filter in to the area, bringing heat index\nvalues below triple digits. For the upcoming work week, it's \ngonna be...you guessed it. Hot. We will remain fixed between \nridging to the west and troughing to the northeast through Monday \nwhich will allow for low chances for diurnally-driven storms. By \nTuesday, high pressure will be solidly back over the southeast, \nshutting off rain chances for a few days. Though it's not \ncurrently looking heat advisory hot (feel-like of 105), it's \nstill going to be uncomfortable out as heat index values make a \nrun for 100 degrees again. Keep this in mind if you have any \noutdoor interests next week. Another pattern shift near the end of\nthe week will re-introduce low rain chances into the forecast.",
